Subject: [PATCH] Phase 6 Milestone 9 - Memory Service Integration Validation
 (GEN-0025)

Validates the complete Memory subsystem integration -- production
Knowledge Graph, Redis Short-Term Memory, Qdrant Vector Memory -- through
the path Milestones 7-8 never exercised: a real Kernel.

No src/ service code needed changes. MemoryService already implemented
Service and already exposed capability_handlers() 'for callers wiring
this into Kernel.register_service()' (src/services/memory/service.py,
pre-existing docstring); Kernel.register_service()/dispatch()/boot()/
shutdown() are all pre-existing public methods, read-only here. This
commit is pure validation, per 'do not redesign existing services' --
the one exception is scripts/run_kernel.py, extended (not replaced) to
demonstrate the same wiring at the existing smoke-test entrypoint.

tests/unit/services/test_memory_integration.py (new, 11 tests):
- MemoryService satisfies the Service Protocol (including on_failure,
  previously untested -- src/services/memory/service.py now at 100%).
- MemoryService registers and boots under a real Kernel; every one of
  the 7 declared capabilities resolves through Kernel.capabilities.
- Kernel.dispatch() drives all three backends -- short-term, vector, and
  knowledge graph -- through a MemoryService built from the same
  production backend classes wire_memory_service() uses
  (RedisShortTermMemory, QdrantVectorMemory, SQLAlchemyKnowledgeGraph),
  with fakeredis / Qdrant local ':memory:' mode standing in for the two
  that need a live network server in production -- the same substitution
  tests/unit/storage/ already established, not mocks of MemoryService's
  own behavior.
- wire_memory_service() composes correctly with a Kernel's own DI
  container (kernel.di), not just a bare standalone DIContainer.
  Full production chain: Kernel -> kernel.di -> wire_memory_service ->
  MemoryService -> register_service -> dispatch.
- dispose_storage() cleans up correctly after a full Kernel boot/dispatch/
  shutdown cycle, is idempotent, and repeated wire_memory_service() calls
  on one container reuse the same built instances rather than duplicating
  connections.

scripts/run_kernel.py (extended): wires the Memory subsystem into
kernel.di via wire_memory_service(), registers it as a real Kernel
service alongside the existing echo service, and dispatches a
memory.graph.add_node@v1/neighbors@v1 call -- verified by running the
script end-to-end.

No graph traversal, graph algorithms, semantic search, embeddings, RAG,
or LLM integration added; Planner, Workflow, Kernel, and Agent Runtime
are all untouched; no new storage backends introduced.

Verified: ruff check, ruff format --check, mypy --strict src/scripts
(63 files), pytest (239 passed, up from 228; 97% coverage, up from 96%)
all clean. src/core/ and src/runtime/ diffs are both empty;
src/storage/, src/services/memory/service.py, interfaces.py,
in_memory.py, and di_wire.py are all unmodified.
